Of course, the decision how to play your wizard is based on stuff like
starting stats and equipment, early findings and so on, but more often
then not I'll find some (studded) leather armor, read some enchantment
scrolls rather then save them all for the AK, and go for the magic
approach. It's fun, and with some carefulness you'll survive. I do have
to watch my PW reserve carefully and have emergency items ready, so I
tend to avoid using too many PW-intensive non-combat spells.

